<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Roderic</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/711">711</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Roderic was the last king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a>, who seized the throne around 710 amid civil strife. In 711 he was defeated and probably killed by the mainly <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tariq-ibn-ziyad">Tariq ibn Ziyad</a> near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guadalete">Guadalete</a> river, opening the Iberian peninsula to the Umayyad conquest. Later Spanish legend made him the subject of tales of betrayal by Count Julian.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/roderic.jpg" alt="Roderic" width="320" height="348" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown Umayyad artist from 8th century. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amra5.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
